cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >
  If you use this template repository in your research, please cite it using
  the metadata below.

title: >
  Synthea-OMOP Synthetic Data Template: Generating Analysis-Specific Synthetic OMOP CDM Datasets
  with Synthea

authors:
  - given-names: "Adam P."
    family-names: "Johnson"
    name-suffix: "MD, MPH"
    affiliation: "Duke University School of Medicine, Department of Surgery"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3014-6372"

repository-code: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/synthea-omop-template"
url: "https://github.com/Duke-Vascular-Informatics/synthea-omop-template"

license: GPL-2.0-only

abstract: >
  A GitHub Template Repository for generating a disease/procedure/outcome-specific
  synthetic OMOP CDM v5.4 dataset with Synthea: author a Synthea module, generate
  synthetic patients, ETL them into OMOP CDM on a SQL Server database, and run
  post-ETL quality checks. The resulting dataset is registered for reuse so that
  analysis repositories (built from strategus-study-template) can develop and test
  against it. It is not used for analysis itself.
  Funding: Research reported in this publication was supported by the National
  Center For Advancing Translational Sciences of the National Institutes of Health
  under Award Number K12TR005435. The content is solely the responsibility of the
  authors and does not necessarily represent the official views of the National
  Institutes of Health.

keywords:
  - OMOP CDM
  - OHDSI
  - synthetic data
  - Synthea
  - clinical informatics
  - reusable template
  - R

references:
